<title>SOUTH KOREA: Commercial Bank 1996 net up 15.2 pct.</title>
<headline>Commercial Bank 1996 net up 15.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in billion won unless stated)</p>
<p>    Share (won)				    620    vs   538</p>
<p>    Net						105.51 vs    91.60</p>
<p>    Dividend (pct, par 5,000 won)		3.0  vs     3.0</p>
<p>    Operating revenue			  3,819.87 vs 3,218.33</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit				 131.36 vs   103.70</p>
<p>Interest Income</p>
<p>	(excluding trust accounts)	   1,880.84 vs 1,553.48</p>
<p>NOTE - The Commercial Bank of Korea is one of South Korea's leading commercial banks. Its share capital was unchanged at 170 million shares at the end of 1996.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
</text>
